# Time-bounded risk record for HIGH findings that have NO upstream fix yet.
# Policy (docs/supply-chain/README.md): no global ignore-unfixed switch; each
# unfixed finding is listed by ID with a reason and an expiry. When an entry
# expires, Trivy reports it again and CI fails until it is re-reviewed or the
# base image digest is bumped to a release that contains the fix.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-10-15 against python:3.12-slim (Debian 13.7) digest
# sha256:a6e34c598f2467ed0e9a8d349809fcd8b5c603269512df273a0bb1784edc11b1.
# Trivy status for every entry below: "affected" or "fix_deferred" (no fixed
# Debian package exists). Anything with a published fix must be upgraded, not
# listed here.
#
# Shared runtime context: the app runs as the unprivileged `app` user with
# cap-drop ALL, no-new-privileges, a read-only root filesystem and no shell
# access; it never invokes mount, nsenter, infocmp, perl or ACL tools.

# util-linux (bsdutils, libblkid1, libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1,
# liblastlog2-2, login, mount, util-linux). All four need SUID mount(8) helper
# options, fstab-authorised bind mounts or nsenter --join-cgroup run by a local
# user. The image has no fstab entries, never runs mount/nsenter, and
# no-new-privileges neutralises SUID. util-linux stays because the entrypoint
# drops privileges with setpriv.
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2027-01-15
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2027-01-15
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2027-01-15
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2027-01-15

# acl (libacl1): symlink traversal in pathname-based libacl calls used by a
# privileged process. Nothing in the image calls libacl on attacker-controlled
# paths, and the app process holds no privilege to escalate from.
CVE-2026-54369 exp:2027-01-15

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin): stack overflow
# in the infocmp CLI only. infocmp is never executed by the service.
CVE-2025-69720 exp:2027-01-15

# systemd (libsystemd0, libudev1): flaw is in the systemd-homed daemon. Only
# the client libraries are present as apt dependencies; no systemd daemon runs.
CVE-2026-16742 exp:2027-01-15

# perl-base: Archive::Tar memory exhaustion on a crafted tar. The service never
# runs Perl or parses tar archives with Archive::Tar. Debian: fix_deferred.
CVE-2026-9538 exp:2027-01-15
